model {
  extend basalt.clientMobile {
    metadata {
      constraint "The foreground phone owns one reconnect attempt at a time across startup, resume, manual reconnect, network events and health checks. Each reconnect has a twelve-second deadline that releases its caller even if a native promise never settles after cancellation. Failed native access validation retries with equal jitter and exponential delays capped at thirty seconds; server-directed Retry-After waits retain their original not-before time across attempt deadlines. An online transition cancels and replaces pending validation when idle; manual Reconnect also cancels the prior attempt before starting fresh. Late cancelled results cannot replace current credential state. Native credential-store operations stay ordered across grant renewal, fresh sign-in and removal even when their original caller cancels; an older write cannot resurrect a signed-out grant or overwrite a new sign-in. Restored server health starts validation immediately when idle; automatic recovery waits for active application work to finish and never aborts or replays it. Backgrounding, explicit disconnect and sign-out cancel recovery. Authoritative authentication refusal stops automatic retries; the existing uncertain rotating-refresh guard still requires a fresh sign-in. A reconnect never replays a model request, tool call or approval. Electron supervises a separate headless client and does not use the phone lifecycle controller."
    }
  }
}
